Subject: The profiler records boolean elements apart from other kinds

What this does
  - `AOT_ELEM_BOOL` marks an element site that loaded or stored a boolean (it was folded into
    `AOT_ELEM_MIXED` before). Profile builds only.

Why we need it
  An array of booleans (a sieve's flags) is a numeric-class array for the inline element access:
  an element is one of int, boolean or double. MIXED also covers strings, undefined and null,
  which are not, so the generator could not tell the two apart.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -1673,6 +1673,7 @@
 #define AOT_ELEM_MIXED  (1u << 3)
 #define AOT_ELEM_HOLEY  (1u << 4)
 #define AOT_ELEM_TA     (1u << 5)  /* a typed array's element */
+#define AOT_ELEM_BOOL   (1u << 6)
 #endif /* QJS_AOT_PROFILE */
 
 /* One polymorphic property cache entry: the receiver shape, the property's
@@ -61890,6 +61891,8 @@
         kind = AOT_ELEM_FLOAT;
     else if (JS_VALUE_GET_TAG(v) == JS_TAG_OBJECT)
         kind = AOT_ELEM_OBJECT;
+    else if (JS_VALUE_GET_TAG(v) == JS_TAG_BOOL)
+        kind = AOT_ELEM_BOOL;
     else
         kind = AOT_ELEM_MIXED;
     if (holey == 2)
